            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No, I am afraid not. I considered not showing it, but there are two good reasons to always do it:\r\n- It reduces flicker when navigating up/down through completion candidates. I.e. it makes info window always shown.\r\n- It shows feedback that info about current completion candidate was already computed and that there is no info to show. In contrast, showing no window introduces a slight moment of contemplation if there was no info window shown already (\"is computation done and there is nothing to show or is it not yet done?\").",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">No, I am afraid not. I considered not showing it, but there are two good reasons to always do it:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>It reduces flicker when navigating up/down through completion candidates. I.e. it makes info window always shown.</li>\n<li>It shows feedback that info about current completion candidate was already computed and that there is no info to show. In contrast, showing no window introduces a slight moment of contemplation if there was no info window shown already (\"is computation done and there is nothing to show or is it not yet done?\").</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "No, I am afraid not. I considered not showing it, but there are two good reasons to always do it:\n\nIt reduces flicker when navigating up/down through completion candidates. I.e. it makes info window always shown.\nIt shows feedback that info about current completion candidate was already computed and that there is no info to show. In contrast, showing no window introduces a slight moment of contemplation if there was no info window shown already (\"is computation done and there is nothing to show or is it not yet done?\").",
